PARITY Music Assistant: the window can load players, browse or search, play on a speaker and transfer a queue
PARITY ListenBrainz and local history: Remember playing, Show remembered, history and recommendations are reachable
PARITY Twitch: Review my follows (explicit import for review) is reachable
PARITY AudioMuse: a station can be made from an AudioMuse mix (generation kind audiomuse)
PARITY Station range (stay_close, in the runbook list "energy, familiarity, speech and range") is settable
PARITY Jellyfin library browses albums, playlists, recently added albums and tracks (runbook); next_listen browses ['albums', 'playlists', 'recent', 'tracks']
PARITY Track details / Play next are reachable: Listen can produce an Audio (track) row from the real Jellyfin browse
PARITY Connections copy only promises what the window can do (no dead promises)
PARITY the capability chips "Plays on speakers" and "History" correspond to a GUI route
PARITY nothing in online_services was orphaned by the removal (every function the classic window called still has a caller)
